# No trailing slash: with one, gitignore matches only a DIRECTORY, and a symlink named node_modules
# (a scratch worktree borrowing the checkout's) was committed by `git add -A` in #426.
node_modules
*.log

# The repository's own hkb directory — the board directory, and a board file if
# HKB_DATABASE_URL points at one here. All of it is local runtime state: a checkout is
# expensive but reproducible, and a binary SQLite board cannot be merged and would be a
# diff nobody can read. The default board is ~/.hkb/board.db, machine-level and outside
# any repository; back it up by copying the file.
#
# `.hkb/workflows/` is the exception, and it is not local at all: a workflow is SOURCE —
# a file whose frontmatter is a Job's spec and whose body is its brief (`src/templates.ts`).
# ADR-015 decision 4 requires hkb's own workflows to come through the same door users get,
# so they live in the repository, get reviewed and merged like anything else, and ship in
# no tarball. `.hkb/*` rather than `.hkb/` because git will not re-include a path underneath
# an excluded DIRECTORY — the negation only works if the directory itself was never excluded.
.hkb/*
!.hkb/workflows/

.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# The publish transpile. Development runs the .ts directly; `npm pack` regenerates this.
/dist/
